# Angular authoring

## File layout

- Component file: kebab-case from export (`bar-chart.ts`)
- Selector: **same as WC tag** (`rd-chart-bar`) for DOM parity
- Standalone component — **no NgModules**
- Spec: `{kebab}.spec.ts`

## Component rules

- `changeDetection: ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush`
- Inputs: `input()` signal API — not `@Input()`
- Outputs: `output()` — not `@Output()` decorator
- Template: inline or external — prefer inline for small atoms matching WC markup
- Control flow: `@if`, `@for` — not `*ngIf` / `*ngFor`
- DI: `inject()` — avoid constructor injection in new code

## CE-host pattern

- `selector: DB_*_TAG` matching WC
- `template: ''` — empty; host element is the CE
- `implements OnInit, OnDestroy`
- Sync `input()` values to attributes in `effect` or `ngOnInit`
- Listen to CE events in `ngOnInit`, remove in `ngOnDestroy`
- `ElementRef<HTMLElement>` for `setProperty` on complex props

## CUSTOM_ELEMENTS_SCHEMA

Required in consuming apps for raw CE tags; runtime components use Angular wrappers — consumers import `@rosettadash/angular/<subpath>`.

## Native Angular components

- Mirror WC BEM in template with matching `data-testid`
- `[ngClass]` / `[class]` for BEM modifiers (e.g. open state)
- `<ng-content />` for default slot position

## Three.js / maps

Full implementations allowed (e.g. `three-geo-globe.ts`) — must dispose on destroy and follow `31-vr-and-3d.mdc`.

## Must not

- NgModule-based declarations in this package
- Different selector than WC tag without parity ticket
- `@Input()` / `@Output()` in new components

